the browser first sends a request to a DNS server

00:30:00.680 --> 00:30:03.680
to look up the IP address of the domain name.

00:30:03.680 --> 00:30:05.680
Step 2, connection.

00:30:05.680 --> 00:30:08.680
Once the browser has the IP address of the website,

00:30:08.680 --> 00:30:12.680
it establishes a connection to the server hosting the website

00:30:12.680 --> 00:30:16.680
using the Hypertext Transfer Protocol, or HTTP.

00:30:16.680 --> 00:30:21.680
Or the more secure HTTPS protocol, the S stands for secure.

00:30:21.680 --> 00:30:23.680
Step 3, request.

00:30:23.680 --> 00:30:25.680
After establishing the connection,

00:30:25.680 --> 00:30:29.680
the browser sends an HTTP request to the server

00:30:29.680 --> 00:30:32.680
requesting the specific webpage or resource

00:30:32.680 --> 00:30:34.680
that the user wants to access.

00:30:34.680 --> 00:30:36.680
Step 4, processing.

00:30:36.680 --> 00:30:40.680
The server receives a request and begins to process it.

00:30:40.680 --> 00:30:44.680
This may involve executing scripts, querying databases,

00:30:44.680 --> 00:30:47.680
and retrieving files from the file system.

00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:49.680
Step 5, response.

00:30:49.680 --> 00:30:52.680
Once the server has processed the request,

00:30:52.680 --> 00:30:55.680
it sends an HTTP response back to the browser.

00:30:55.680 --> 00:30:58.680
This response includes the requested content,

00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:01.680
such as the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript,

00:31:01.680 --> 00:31:06.680
and any images or other resources required to display the website.

00:31:06.680 --> 00:31:08.680
Step 6, rendering.

00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:11.680
The browser receives the response from the server

00:31:11.680 --> 00:31:13.680
and begins to render the webpage.

00:31:13.680 --> 00:31:16.680
This involves parsing the HTML and rendering the layout,

00:31:16.680 --> 00:31:19.680
styling the page with CSS, executing JavaScript,

00:31:19.680 --> 00:31:22.680
and loading any images or other resources

00:31:22.680 --> 00:31:24.680
required to display the page.

00:31:24.680 --> 00:31:27.680
Step 7, user interaction.

00:31:27.680 --> 00:31:30.680
Finally, the user can interact with the webpage,

00:31:30.680 --> 00:31:32.680
clicking on links, filling out forms,

00:31:32.680 --> 00:31:34.680
and performing other actions.

00:31:34.680 --> 00:31:36.680
These steps happen very quickly,

00:31:36.680 --> 00:31:38.680
often in a matter of milliseconds,

00:31:38.680 --> 00:31:41.680
but any delay or bottleneck in any of these steps

00:31:41.680 --> 00:31:44.680
can cause the page to load slowly or not at all,

00:31:44.680 --> 00:31:47.680
leading to a poor user experience.

00:31:47.680 --> 00:31:49.680
To optimize website performance,

00:31:49.680 --> 00:31:52.680
it's important to identify and address any performance issues

00:31:52.680 --> 00:31:56.680
at each stage of the process.

